# Component Layers

One-way dependencies: `src` → `biz-ui` → `design-system` → `utils`. `src` may also import `design-system` and `utils` directly.

- `packages/design-system` (`@landing-page/design-system`): atomic UI with no business meaning (Button, Input, Card).
- `packages/biz-ui` (`@landing-page/biz-ui`): reusable composed UI. Data, routing, and auth come in through props or slots. May depend on `@landing-page/design-system`, `@landing-page/utils`, and `react`. Must not depend on `next`, `next-themes`, `next-auth`, Lingui, tRPC, Zustand, `@/`, `~/server`, `mastra-server`, or app infrastructure such as Vercel Analytics.
- `src/`: routes, tRPC, Zustand, Lingui, NextAuth, and page-only UI in `src/app/.../_components`.

Put a new reusable composed component in `biz-ui` directly. Extract from `src` only at the second use: drop `@/` imports, turn hooks, store, and i18n into props, then switch the import. Leave single-route UI in `_components`. Do not bulk-migrate `src/components`.

A chat bubble shell that only takes `role` and `children` belongs in `biz-ui`. A `ThemeSwitcher` that calls `useTheme()` stays in `src` until it accepts `theme` and `onThemeChange`.
